From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:32:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] fix(wlan): advertise the basic rates of the MT8163 access
 point

The setup hotspot (ADR 0028) came up on an Echo Dot (2nd gen) running
0.5.0-beta.1, but every client was refused at association with status
18: it doesn't support all of the BSS basic rates. A phone said "failed
to join"; a Linux client logged CTRL-EVENT-ASSOC-REJECT status_code=18
four times, and hostapd never saw a station.

The P2P init sets up the BSS for 11G_P2P and fills the rates the beacon
advertises from it: 6(B) 9 12(B) 18 24(B) 36 48 54, which is what a scan
of the hotspot showed. When hostapd starts a pure access point,
p2pFuncStartGO switches the BSS to mixed 11b/g, whose basic rates are 1,
2, 5.5 and 11 Mbit/s, but rebuilds the advertised rates only in OOBE AP
mode, which Pinna leaves off. A client offers only rates it saw in the
beacon, so it never offers the 11b basic rates, and the association
check refuses it.

Rebuild the advertised rates for a pure access point too, so the beacon
lists 1(B) 2(B) 5.5(B) 11(B) and the OFDM rates. The station side and
the P2P group owner path are unchanged.

Not built or run on a device yet.
---
 .../conn_soc/drv_wlan/mt_wifi/wlan/mgmt/p2p_func.c       | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/mt8163-connectivity/conn_soc/drv_wlan/mt_wifi/wlan/mgmt/p2p_func.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/mt8163-connectivity/conn_soc/drv_wlan/mt_wifi/wlan/mgmt/p2p_func.c
index d85a24d..71b28c7 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/mt8163-connectivity/conn_soc/drv_wlan/mt_wifi/wlan/mgmt/p2p_func.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/mt8163-connectivity/conn_soc/drv_wlan/mt_wifi/wlan/mgmt/p2p_func.c
@@ -413,7 +413,14 @@ p2pFuncStartGO(IN P_ADAPTER_T prAdapter,
 		prBssInfo->u2OperationalRateSet =
 		    rNonHTPhyAttributes[prBssInfo->ucNonHTBasicPhyType].u2SupportedRateSet;
 
-		if (prBssInfo->ucAllSupportedRatesLen == 0 || fgIsOOBEAP) {
+		/* The rates the beacon advertises must follow the basic rates set
+		 * above. The P2P init filled them for 11G_P2P (OFDM only), and a
+		 * pure AP switches to mixed 11b/g, whose basic rates are 1, 2, 5.5
+		 * and 11 Mbit/s. Kept from init, the beacon offered only OFDM
+		 * rates, clients offered no others, and every association was
+		 * refused with status 18 (Echo Dot (2nd gen), 2026-11-20).
+		 */
+		if (prBssInfo->ucAllSupportedRatesLen == 0 || fgIsOOBEAP || fgIsPureAP) {
 			rateGetDataRatesFromRateSet(prBssInfo->u2OperationalRateSet,
 						    prBssInfo->u2BSSBasicRateSet,
 						    prBssInfo->aucAllSupportedRates,
-- 
